# prof-DA done-gate

Cursor has no turn-level Stop hook, so this rule carries the gate. Before claiming ANY deliverable done
(done / fixed / passing / shipped), run the portable gate and show the exit code:

    python adapters/gate.py .prof-da/pending-validation.json    # set PROFDA_GATE to the plugin's gate.py if out-of-tree

exit 0 = every named deliverable exists + is non-empty + (code) proven, AND the project's requirement
monitor has no OPEN ask left un-cleared by a fresh all-MET review receipt. Nonzero = NOT done (build /
reconcile first). A task is not done until this passes - see `skills/da/references/evidence-based-done.md`.
